Lab 3: Importing Existing Clusters into RHACM
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Understand the cluster import process in Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management (RHACM)
Import existing OpenShift clusters into RHACM using the oc CLI
Configure cluster import settings and authentication
Monitor and verify the health status of imported clusters
Troubleshoot common cluster import issues
Manage imported clusters through the RHACM console
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, ensure you have:

Basic knowledge of OpenShift Container Platform
Familiarity with Kubernetes concepts and kubectl/oc CLI commands
Understanding of YAML configuration files
Access to at least two OpenShift clusters (one hub cluster with RHACM installed, one managed cluster to import)
Cluster administrator privileges on both clusters
Network connectivity between the hub cluster and the cluster to be imported
