Task 1: Prepare for Cluster Import
Subtask 1.1: Verify Hub Cluster Access
First, let's ensure you have access to your RHACM hub cluster and verify the installation.

Connect to the hub cluster:
# Set the hub cluster context
oc login --server=https://api.hub-cluster.example.com:6443 --username=admin --password=your-password

# Verify you're connected to the correct cluster
oc whoami
oc cluster-info
Verify RHACM installation:
# Check if RHACM operator is installed
oc get operators -A | grep advanced-cluster-management

# Verify RHACM pods are running
oc get pods -n open-cluster-management

# Check MultiClusterHub status
oc get multiclusterhub -n open-cluster-management
Access RHACM console:
# Get the RHACM console route
oc get route multicloud-console -n open-cluster-management -o jsonpath='{.spec.host}'
Subtask 1.2: Verify Target Cluster Access
Now, let's verify access to the cluster you want to import.

Connect to the target cluster:
# Set the managed cluster context
oc login --server=https://api.managed-cluster.example.com:6443 --username=admin --password=your-password

# Verify cluster access and get cluster information
oc whoami
oc get nodes
oc get clusterversion
Check cluster readiness:
# Verify cluster operators are available
oc get co

# Check cluster resources
oc get namespaces
oc top nodes
Note cluster details for import:
# Get cluster API server URL
oc whoami --show-server

# Get cluster name
oc get infrastructure cluster -o jsonpath='{.status.infrastructureName}'
Task 2: Import Cluster Using oc CLI
Subtask 2.1: Create ManagedCluster Resource
Switch back to your hub cluster and create the necessary resources to import the target cluster.

Switch to hub cluster context:
# Return to hub cluster
oc login --server=https://api.hub-cluster.example.com:6443 --username=admin --password=your-password

# Verify you're on the hub cluster
oc get multiclusterhub -n open-cluster-management
Create ManagedCluster resource:
# Create a YAML file for the ManagedCluster
cat > managed-cluster-import.yaml << EOF
apiVersion: cluster.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: ManagedCluster
metadata:
  name: imported-cluster-01
  labels:
    cloud: auto-detect
    vendor: auto-detect
    environment: production
    region: us-east-1
spec:
  hubAcceptsClient: true
  leaseDurationSeconds: 60
EOF

# Apply the ManagedCluster resource
oc apply -f managed-cluster-import.yaml
Verify ManagedCluster creation:
# Check if the ManagedCluster was created
oc get managedcluster imported-cluster-01

# View detailed information
oc describe managedcluster imported-cluster-01
Subtask 2.2: Generate Import Command
Generate the import command that will be executed on the target cluster.

Create KlusterletAddonConfig:
# Create addon configuration for the managed cluster
cat > klusterlet-addon-config.yaml << EOF
apiVersion: agent.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: KlusterletAddonConfig
metadata:
  name: imported-cluster-01
  namespace: imported-cluster-01
spec:
  clusterName: imported-cluster-01
  clusterNamespace: imported-cluster-01
  clusterLabels:
    cloud: auto-detect
    vendor: auto-detect
  applicationManager:
    enabled: true
  policyController:
    enabled: true
  searchCollector:
    enabled: true
  certPolicyController:
    enabled: true
  iamPolicyController:
    enabled: true
EOF

# Apply the addon configuration
oc apply -f klusterlet-addon-config.yaml
Generate import secret:
# Get the import secret from the managed cluster namespace
oc get secret -n imported-cluster-01 imported-cluster-01-import -o jsonpath='{.data.import\.yaml}' | base64 -d > import-command.yaml

# View the generated import command
cat import-command.yaml
Alternative method - Generate import command directly:
# Use RHACM CLI to generate import command
oc get secret -n imported-cluster-01 imported-cluster-01-import -o jsonpath='{.data.crds\.yaml}' | base64 -d > import-crds.yaml
oc get secret -n imported-cluster-01 imported-cluster-01-import -o jsonpath='{.data.import\.yaml}' | base64 -d > import-resources.yaml
Subtask 2.3: Execute Import on Target Cluster
Now switch to the target cluster and execute the import command.

Switch to target cluster:
# Connect to the managed cluster
oc login --server=https://api.managed-cluster.example.com:6443 --username=admin --password=your-password

# Verify connection
oc whoami --show-server
Apply import resources:
# First apply CRDs if using separate files
oc apply -f import-crds.yaml

# Apply the import resources
oc apply -f import-resources.yaml

# Or if using single file
# oc apply -f import-command.yaml
Verify klusterlet installation:
# Check if open-cluster-management-agent namespace was created
oc get namespace open-cluster-management-agent

# Verify klusterlet pods are running
oc get pods -n open-cluster-management-agent

# Check klusterlet status
oc get klusterlet -A
