Subtask 3.3: Test Cluster Management Capabilities
Test basic management operations on the imported cluster.

Create a test namespace on managed cluster:
# Create a namespace through RHACM
cat > test-namespace.yaml << EOF
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: rhacm-test
  labels:
    managed-by: rhacm
---
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: PlacementRule
metadata:
  name: test-placement
  namespace: rhacm-test
spec:
  clusterSelector:
    matchLabels:
      name: imported-cluster-01
---
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: Subscription
metadata:
  name: test-subscription
  namespace: rhacm-test
spec:
  channel: rhacm-test/test-channel
  placement:
    placementRef:
      name: test-placement
      kind: PlacementRule
EOF

# Apply the test resources
oc apply -f test-namespace.yaml
Verify deployment on managed cluster:
# Switch to managed cluster to verify
oc login --server=https://api.managed-cluster.example.com:6443 --username=admin --password=your-password

# Check if namespace was created
oc get namespace rhacm-test

# Verify RHACM agents are working
oc get pods -n open-cluster-management-agent
Test policy deployment:
# Switch back to hub cluster
oc login --server=https://api.hub-cluster.example.com:6443 --username=admin --password=your-password

# Create a simple policy
cat > test-policy.yaml << EOF
apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: Policy
metadata:
  name: test-namespace-policy
  namespace: imported-cluster-01
spec:
  remediationAction: inform
  disabled: false
  policy-templates:
    - objectDefinition:
        apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
        kind: ConfigurationPolicy
        metadata:
          name: test-namespace-config
        spec:
          remediationAction: inform
          severity: low
          object-templates:
            - complianceType: musthave
              objectDefinition:
                apiVersion: v1
                kind: Namespace
                metadata:
                  name: policy-test-namespace
EOF

# Apply the test policy
oc apply -f test-policy.yaml

# Check policy status
oc get policy -n imported-cluster-01
Task 4: Advanced Cluster Management and Monitoring
Subtask 4.1: Configure Cluster Labels and Annotations
Enhance cluster management by adding meaningful labels and annotations.

Add cluster labels:
# Add environment label
oc label managedcluster imported-cluster-01 environment=production

# Add location label
oc label managedcluster imported-cluster-01 location=datacenter-east

# Add team ownership label
oc label managedcluster imported-cluster-01 team=platform-engineering

# Verify labels
oc get managedcluster imported-cluster-01 --show-labels
Add cluster annotations:
# Add annotations for additional metadata
oc annotate managedcluster imported-cluster-01 import-date="$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
oc annotate managedcluster imported-cluster-01 imported-by="$(oc whoami)"
oc annotate managedcluster imported-cluster-01 cluster-purpose="production-workloads"

# View annotations
oc get managedcluster imported-cluster-01 -o yaml | grep -A 10 annotations
Subtask 4.2: Set Up Cluster Monitoring and Alerting
Configure monitoring and alerting for the imported cluster.

Enable observability addons:
# Check if observability is available
oc get multiclusterobservability -A

# Enable metrics collection
oc patch klusterletaddonconfig imported-cluster-01 -n imported-cluster-01 --type='merge' -p='{"spec":{"searchCollector":{"enabled":true}}}'

# Verify addon status
oc get managedclusteraddons -n imported-cluster-01
Create cluster monitoring dashboard:
# Create a custom resource for cluster monitoring
cat > cluster-monitoring.yaml << EOF
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: cluster-monitoring-config
  namespace: imported-cluster-01
data:
  config.yaml: |
    enableUserWorkloadMonitoring: true
    prometheusK8s:
      retention: 7d
      resources:
        requests:
          cpu: 100m
          memory: 1Gi
EOF

# Apply monitoring configuration
oc apply -f cluster-monitoring.yaml
Subtask 4.3: Implement Cluster Backup and Disaster Recovery
Set up backup and recovery procedures for the imported cluster.

Create cluster backup policy:
# Create backup policy
cat > cluster-backup-policy.yaml << EOF
apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: Policy
metadata:
  name: cluster-backup-policy
  namespace: imported-cluster-01
spec:
  remediationAction: enforce
  disabled: false
  policy-templates:
    - objectDefinition:
        apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
        kind: ConfigurationPolicy
        metadata:
          name: etcd-backup-config
        spec:
          remediationAction: enforce
          severity: high
          object-templates:
            - complianceType: musthave
              objectDefinition:
                apiVersion: v1
                kind: CronJob
                metadata:
                  name: etcd-backup
                  namespace: openshift-etcd
                spec:
                  schedule: "0 2 * * *"
                  jobTemplate:
                    spec:
                      template:
                        spec:
                          containers:
                          - name: etcd-backup
                            image: registry.redhat.io/ubi8/ubi:latest
                            command:
                            - /bin/bash
                            - -c
                            - echo "Backup job placeholder"
                          restartPolicy: OnFailure
EOF

# Apply backup policy
oc apply -f cluster-backup-policy.yaml
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Cluster Import Fails
Symptoms: ManagedCluster shows as unavailable or import command fails

Solutions:

# Check network connectivity
oc get managedcluster imported-cluster-01 -o yaml | grep -A 5 conditions

# Verify certificates
oc get secret -n imported-cluster-01 | grep import

# Check klusterlet logs on managed cluster
oc logs -n open-cluster-management-agent deployment/klusterlet
Issue 2: Addons Not Working
Symptoms: ManagedClusterAddons show as degraded

Solutions:

# Check addon status
oc get managedclusteraddons -n imported-cluster-01

# Restart addon pods
oc delete pods -n open-cluster-management-agent -l app=klusterlet

# Verify addon configuration
oc describe klusterletaddonconfig imported-cluster-01 -n imported-cluster-01
Issue 3: Policy Not Applied
Symptoms: Policies remain in pending or non-compliant state

Solutions:

# Check policy status
oc describe policy test-namespace-policy -n imported-cluster-01

# Verify policy controller
oc get pods -n open-cluster-management-agent | grep governance

# Check placement rules
oc get placementrule -A
